  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Mastering Tap Timing Basics",
        "body": "Every quest in Treasure Cruise is fundamentally won or lost on tap timing accuracy. Each crew member displays a tap window during their attack animation; PERFECT taps land within the last 10% of the swing arc. Begin practicing with slower characters (less agile fighters like Whitebeard or Big Mom) before the tap cadence becomes natural. Once consistent PERFECT taps feel reliable, focus on chain lock strategies that freeze the window for the entire crew."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Building Your First Legend Team",
        "body": "A competitive Legend team requires: 1 captain with a Chain Lock ability (prevents chain from resetting), 1 captain with a damage multiplier for the team's primary color type, and 4 crew members that match the color type for consistent chain contribution. The Friend Captain system allows using another player's maxed legend captain without owning the unit; select Friend Captains with complementary abilities to your own captain for effectively doubled multipliers."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Kizuna Clash and Coliseum",
        "body": "Kizuna Clash events (PvP cooperation raids) and Coliseum quests are the primary sources of end-game power items. Kizuna Clash provides Luffy manuals and rare evolution materials from cooperative boss kills; join an active crew that coordinates Kizuna attacks for maximum damage output. Coliseum provides unique units and skill books; completing all Coliseum quest difficulties (INT, DEX, QCK, STR, PSY) is required for completion-focused players."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Not leveling Friend Points (FP) characters for early support roles—FP pulls provide key support units (Coby, Helmeppo) that fill team gaps cheaply before Legend availability.",
      "Using gems on standard banners instead of Sugo-Fest—standard banner Legendary rate is ~2%; Sugo-Fest rate can reach 5% or higher; patience with gems for Sugo-Fest dramatically improves Legend acquisition.",
      "Not socket-boarding key units—Sockets (from Pirate Rumble rewards) provide Bind, Despair, and Silence resistance; characters without appropriate sockets are frequently locked out of action in high-difficulty content.",
